# Corpus — ignore what we can't redistribute (someone else's fetched content)
# or what's large/rebuildable. Derived-ness alone is NOT the criterion.
# (gitignore has no inline comments — keep patterns on their own lines.)
# data/raw/ and data/processed/: third-party HTML/Markdown — redistribution constraint.
data/raw/
data/processed/
# data/chunks.jsonl is derived too, but carries no redistribution constraint and is
# small (748K) — TRACKED so the reasoned taxonomy is diffable without running Python.

# Vector store + sparse index (both derived, large/rebuildable)
chroma_db/
data/bm25.pkl

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets
.env

# eval run artifact (volatile results)
eval/last_run.json
eval_run.log
eval/answer_partial_review.md
